# Project Context Template

Use for stable task-relevant facts worth preserving. Prefer an existing project overview; do not inventory the whole repository or treat this unfilled template as known context.

## Scope and freshness

Record the project/area, applicable revision or content version, date checked, and limits of the discovery. Identify what would make these facts stale.

## Confirmed facts

| Fact | Source or observation | Version/date applicability |
| --- | --- | --- |

Include purpose, affected behavior, ownership, consumers, and constraints only where supported. Distinguish declared, installed, and proposed versions if relevant.

## Verification path

| Criterion | Check or scenario | Source, cwd, prerequisites | Execution status/evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |

Record actual project commands or suitable review/walkthrough scenarios. Mark unavailable commands as unknown; finding a command is not executing it.

## Assumptions and gaps

Name unsupported assumptions, missing evidence, and the smallest useful next lookup. Keep credentials and private raw data out of shared records.
